---
// src/pages/terms.astro
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="Terms of service, fair usage policies, and liability disclaimers for the GovtRecruitments government opportunities discovery platform."
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16">
    <div class="bg-card rounded-3xl p-8 sm:p-12 border border-border shadow-sm">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-bold bg-purple-50 text-purple-900 border border-purple-200 uppercase tracking-wider mb-4">
        Platform Terms
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-2xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-foreground mb-6">
        Terms of Use
      </h1>

      <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none text-sm text-muted-foreground space-y-6 leading-relaxed">
        <p class="text-base text-foreground font-medium">
          Welcome to GovtRecruitments. By accessing or utilizing this website, you agree to comply with and be bound by the following Terms of Use.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-foreground pt-4">
          1. Advisory & Informational Nature
        </h2>
        <p>
          GovtRecruitments is an algorithmic discovery tool intended to help aspirants navigate public recruitment notices. The evaluation generated by the Eligibility Engine is an analytical interpretation based on verified gazette parameters. It does NOT constitute a legal admission guarantee, provisional acceptance, or official certificate of eligibility from any recruiting agency.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-foreground pt-4">
          2. Candidate Responsibility
        </h2>
        <p>
          Every candidate is solely responsible for verifying their personal eligibility against the official recruitment notification PDF before submitting applications or paying exam fees. GovtRecruitments accepts no liability for missed deadlines, rejected applications, or discrepancies arising from official board corrigenda.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-foreground pt-4">
          3. Intellectual Property & Official Gazette Rights
        </h2>
        <p>
          All underlying recruitment notifications, syllabi, rulebooks, government emblems, and advertisement texts belong strictly to their respective central, state, or union-territory statutory authorities. The GovtRecruitments code, design system, deterministic evaluation algorithms, and curated taxonomies are protected by intellectual property laws.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-foreground pt-4">
          4. Fair Usage & Automated Scraping
        </h2>
        <p>
          You agree not to disrupt the platform through denial-of-service attempts, aggressive automated scraping without prior permission, or injecting malicious payloads. Automated access to GovtRecruitments APIs or web pages must adhere to standard <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-foreground font-mono">robots.txt</code> directives and rate limits.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-foreground pt-4">
          5. Modifications to Terms
        </h2>
        <p>
          GovtRecruitments reserves the right to revise these Terms of Use at any time. Material changes will be noted on this page along with an updated timestamp. Continued use of the platform after modifications indicates your acceptance.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
